# Resort Frontend API

Give this file to frontend. All paths are relative to the base URL.

**Base URL:** `http://116.193.129.229:8092/api`

---

## How to call

Always send **raw JSON**. Do not use `form-data` or `x-www-form-urlencoded`.

```
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {token}
```

`Authorization` is required on every route except `POST /login`.

### Status codes

| Code | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `200` | Success (list, details, update, delete) |
| `201` | Created (add) |
| `400` | Business error (`Error_Code: 1`) |
| `401` | Missing or invalid token |
| `404` | Record not found |
| `422` | Validation error |

### Success (create / update / delete)

```json
{
  "Error_Code": 0,
  "Message": "Reservation created successfully.",
  "data": {}
}
```

### Business error

```json
{
  "Error_Code": 1,
  "Message": "Room is already booked.",
  "data": null
}
```

If `Error_Code` is `1`, show `Message` to the user.

### Validation error `422`

```json
{
  "message": "The given data was invalid.",
  "errors": {
    "guest_name": ["The guest name field is required."]
  }
}
```

### Unauthenticated `401`

```json
{ "message": "Unauthenticated." }
```

